course: dictionary
lesson: 8911
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Siberian can mean three different things, so context matters. Most of the time it is a place word. Siberia is the huge, very cold northern part of Russia, stretching from the Ural Mountains to the Pacific Ocean. «Siberian peoples such as the Khanty, Evenks and Yakuts lost land» tells you these are people from that region.
explain: Put Siberian before an animal or plant name and it tells you where that creature comes from. «Siberian tiger» is a tiger from Siberia, and «Siberian husky» is a dog from there. The name shows the place, not a special kind of tiger or dog. Ask yourself: what is the rest of the phrase naming?
explain: Siberian can also mean extremely cold, as in «a Siberian wind». In weather news, «Siberian blast» means freezing air. Check the sentence: if the place does not fit, the word is probably describing the cold.
fact: Siberian is an adjective (a Siberian wind) and a noun (a Siberian, Siberians), which means a person from Siberia.
fact: Siberia is a huge, very cold part of northern Russia, from the Ural Mountains to the Pacific Ocean.
fact: Lake Baikal, in Siberia, is the deepest lake in the world.
fact: The Siberian tiger is the largest cat, and it is endangered.
fact: Siberian huskies pull sleds, and «Siberian winter» can mean a winter that is bitterly cold.
exercise: In «Siberian tiger», what does Siberian tell you? | *The tiger comes from Siberia | The tiger lives in a zoo | The tiger is very cold to touch | The tiger has a tiny tail
exercise: «A Siberian blast swept in from the east.» What does Siberian mean here? | Made of wood | Very sunny and warm | From a family called Siberian | *Extremely cold
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Siberian peoples such as the Khanty, Evenks and Yakuts lost land» that names a group of people. | land | lost | Siberian | *Khanty
test: Which of these is the name of a dog breed from Siberia? | Siberian tiger | Siberian blast | Siberian winter | *Siberian husky
test: In «woolly mammoths frozen in Siberian ice», what does Siberian tell you? | The ice is pink and sweet | The ice is thick and cracked | The ice is a kind of lake | *The ice is from Siberia
exam: Jayden says Siberian always means very cold. Is he right, and why? | *No, it can mean from or about Siberia, as in «Siberian husky», or extremely cold, as in «Siberian blast» | Yes, because Siberia is always warm | No, it only ever means a type of tiger | Yes, it always means cold, whatever the sentence says
